# Content

Studio copy, people, and works live in `src/content/` as JSON (MDX only when a long story needs it). All three UI versions read the same files. Do not fork content per version. Components do not embed bios, credits, or theme colors.

The JSON files below are the content source. Do not invent fields, and do not copy the discarded paper-label copy (stand-in project titles, a services menu, or an inquiry line).

Placeholder strings stay marked placeholder. Do not present stand-in titles as finished studio work.

## Files

Files:

- `talents.json` — people
- `releases.json` — songs
- `artworks.json` — stills
- `animations.json` — motion pieces
- `site.json` — nav, socials, studio story, exhibition entries

## Shapes

Talent:

```json
{
  "slug": "sasayaka-lumi",
  "name": "Sasayaka Lumi",
  "nameJp": "",
  "unit": "Eonica",
  "themeColor": "",
  "avatar": "",
  "portrait": "",
  "fanName": "",
  "oshiMark": "",
  "birthday": "",
  "height": "",
  "debut": "",
  "languages": [],
  "bio": "",
  "lore": "",
  "socials": { "youtube": "", "twitch": "", "x": "", "tiktok": "" }
}
```

Leave `themeColor` and `lore` empty until Kaung supplies them. A hover bio may be the placeholder "Dummy bio." Do not guess a hex.

Release fields: `slug`, `title`, `talentSlugs[]`, `type` (`cover` | `original` | `unit`), `date`, `jacket`, `credits[{role, name}]`, optional `audioSrc`, `peaks`, `lyrics` (timed lines), `mvYoutubeId`, `streamingLinks[]`. The saved Kamitsubaki pages do not show a working filter. `mixitup.js` is loaded and never called. Building a filter is new. Do not claim it was copied from those HTML files.

The profile fields (fan name, oshi mark, birthday, height, debut, lore) come from the brief. No Chizu HTML is in `resource/`. Leave them empty until Kaung supplies them.

Artwork: `slug`, `title`, `artist`, `category` (`talent-design` | `fan-art` | `key-visual` | `sketch`), `image`, `width`, `height`, `alt`, optional `process[]` (`sketch` | `line` | `color`), `tags[]`, `date`.

Animation: `slug`, `title`, `poster`, `video`, optional `youtubeId`, `credits[]`, `storyboardFrames[]`, `frameSequence` `{path, count}`, `bts[]`.

Site: `nav`, `socials`, `story`, `exhibition[]`. Socials and contact are email and Discord only. No inquiry form.

Lyrics are an array of `{ "t": 0, "line": "" }` in seconds. The line highlight reads this file. The words also render as plain text when audio is off.

## Add a work without code

1. Put the image, audio, or video in `public/assets/arri/`. Reference scraps stay in `public/assets/ref/` and are listed in `ASSETS.md`.
2. Add one object to the matching JSON file. Reuse an existing `slug` style: lowercase, hyphenated.
3. Point `image`, `jacket`, `poster`, or `video` at that file. Set `width` and `height` for every still.
4. For a song, set `talentSlugs` to slugs that already exist in `talents.json`, and set `type`.
5. For a still with a process reveal, add `process` in order: sketch, line, color.
6. Do not add a route, a component, or a nav item. The pages read the collection.

A talent with an empty name stays out of the grid. A work with `dummy: true` stays visible and is labeled Dummy. Show a quiet empty state when a collection has no entries.

